('PI-ING-002171','oligofructose_fos_p95_global','OLIGOFRUCTOSE (FOS) · P95 · 95% SOLIDS · Powder','Standard','Standard','General','','fiber','oligofructose_fos','TRUE','TRUE','Estimated / PI Calculated','GC-04 global form/grade reference | GC53 available carbohydrate excludes fibre','2026-09-08','88','5','95','0','0','0','0','0','0','4.75','4.75','4.75','0','0','0','0','0','90.25','0','0','0','0','','95','28.5','70.3','','0.285','0.703','0','','','199.5','','','none_declared','TRUE','TRUE','TRUE','FALSE','ambient_dry','','Brand-neutral oligofructose/FOS powder reference: ~95% solids, ~95% oligofructose on dry basis and ~5% free sugars. Pure oligofructose sweetness is ~30% of sucrose. | GC53 CORRECTION: Corrected double-count: availableC is free sugar residual only; fibre remains separate. Free sugars sucrose-equivalent model, not exact spectrum. Existing custom POD/PAC retained (not revalidated here). Energy computed4*availableC+2*fibre.','ENGINE-APPROVED GLOBAL SUGAR-REPLACEMENT SOLIDS PI. Category remains fiber because the primary function is soluble fiber/bulking; POD/PAC support Rescue. | GC53 ACTIVE CONVENTION: carbohydrate_percent excludes fibre. Do not count the free-sugar pool twice; sucrose_percent is an equivalent surrogate. Original POD/PAC retained as family reference, not new analytical validation. Energy4kcal/g available carb +2kcal/g fibre is calculation convention; actual PR calorie declaration overrides.','https://jn.nutrition.org/article/S0022-3166%2823%2902107-7/fulltext | https://academic.oup.com/ijfst/article/43/9/1520/7864639','','Gellatti · GC53 household and structure audit','2026-09-08'),
