('PI-ING-002173','global_milk_0_1_fat_pasteurized_uht','MILK · 0.1% FAT · Pasteurized/UHT','Standard','Standard','General','','dairy','milk','TRUE','TRUE','Estimated / PI Calculated','GC11-12 GLOBAL REFERENCE: MILK','2026-09-07','85','90.5442','9.4558','0.1','0.064','0.1','9.3558','3.5344','3.5344','4.9898','4.9898','0','0','0','0','4.9898','0','0','0.1','0','0.8316','','','9.4558','0.7984','5.5748','','0.16','1.1172','0','','','35','','','milk','FALSE','FALSE','TRUE','FALSE','refrigerated','','GLOBAL, brand-neutral; not an exact SKU. Fat-standardized milk; protein/carbohydrate/ash derived by skim-phase scaling from Tetra Pak reference milk. Saturated fat modelled from family fraction. Owner convention: 100 ml = 100 g; no density adjustment. This is a reference profile, not a statistical world average. Allergens describe the defined ingredient; no unsupported brand-specific trace claims. Confidence is an editorial evidence score, not a statistical probability or certification.','GC11-12 data-only. Water by mass balance using estimated ash; salt is already part of mineral fraction, not added twice. POD/PAC use existing Mapper coefficients (including salt contribution). Missing analytical sugar speciation is modelled and disclosed. Aerating protein is a composition proxy, not a measured foaming capacity. Exact product facts take precedence. No application/Engine/Rescue execution or code change performed.','https://dairyprocessinghandbook.tetrapak.com/chapter/chemistry-milk','','Gellatti · GC11-12 Dairy data audit','2026-09-07'),
