('PI-ING-002440','global_nat11_cocoa_powder','NATURAL COCOA POWDER · 11% FAT · Unsweetened','Standard','Standard','General','','chocolate','natural_cocoa_powder','TRUE','TRUE','Estimated / PI Calculated','GC51: defined formula / reference composition; details in material and source worksheets','2026-09-08','86','3','97','11','6.479562','0','0','20.235294','0','21.577431','1.806723','1.806723','0','0','0','0','0','38.19928','0.054202','0','5.987995','','','97','1.806723','2.123803','','0.018067','0.021238','0','','','342.64946','','','none_declared','TRUE','TRUE','TRUE','FALSE','ambient_dry','','Defined fat-standardized unsweetened cocoa-powder model. Nonfat phase derived from USDA natural/alkalized reference; not a producer assay. Sugar species represented as sucrose-equivalent because a complete analytical spectrum is not supplied. Formula per 100g: NAT11=100.000000g.','GC51 reference data, not a measured SKU or statistically sampled worldwide average. Sugar chemistry uses the existing Mapper coefficients and weighted donor POD/PAC, including accepted maltitol when applicable. Carbohydrate excludes separately recorded fibre; polyols are part of carbohydrate; salt is part of ash and is not counted twice in mass. Milk aerating protein is an inherited composition proxy, not an assay after chocolate processing. Cocoa dry solids are documented in the name/calculation, without adding a main-schema column. Exact PR label/composition takes precedence. 100ml=100g owner convention unchanged. No app, importer, Engine, Rescue or finished-product trial was executed. Product process/cross-contact remains supplier-dependent.','https://www.ars.usda.gov/ARSUserFiles/80400535/Data/SR/SR28/reports/sr28fg19.pdf#page=324 | https://www.callebaut.com/en/cacao-powder','','Gellatti · GC51 Cocoa/Chocolate data audit','2026-09-08'),
