('PI-ING-002550','global_hojicha_powder_dry_no_carrier','HOJICHA · Roasted Green Tea Powder · Dry · No Carrier','Standard','Standard','General','','coffee_tea','tea_hojicha_powder','TRUE','TRUE','Estimated / Source-based global reference','MEXT Japanese Standard Tables item 16063 dry hojicha tea + current pure hojicha powder identity/label cross-check; GC65 PI calculation','2026-09-09','92','1.8','98.2','5','1.2','0','0','18.4','0','10.1','4','0','0','0','0','0','0','49.3','0.00762','0','4.7','','','98.2','4','4.044577','','0.04','0.04044577','0','','','257','','','none_declared','TRUE','TRUE','TRUE','FALSE','ambient_dry','','GLOBAL DEFINED REFERENCE. Pure finely milled roasted Japanese green tea; no sugar, milk or carrier added to the ingredient identity. Distinct from PI-ING-002487 prepared hojicha infusion and from instant tea extract. When the powder remains in the recipe, count the full retained composition; when tea solids are strained out, use the final prepared infusion profile. Exact commercial label/TDS overrides this global reference.','GC65 ENGINE-APPROVED GLOBAL PI. Core water/protein/fat/available carbohydrate/fibre/ash/energy values come from MEXT dry hojicha tea item 16063. Grinding changes particle size, not the whole-material mass composition. MEXT total solids include approximately 10.7 g/100 g of tea solids not represented by the current macro fields; the source identifies caffeine and tannin as the principal omitted fractions. Saturated fat 1.2 g/100 g and total sugars 4.0 g/100 g are a current pure 100% hojicha powder label cross-check, not a universal batch specification. Sugar species are not declared; POD/PAC use the aggregate sugars as a sucrose-equivalent proxy plus the existing salt factor. Caffeine, tannins, polyphenols and mineral species are not separately parameterized and do not receive additional guessed PAC. Exact product TDS overrides all modeled priors.','https://fooddb.mext.go.jp/details/details.pl?ITEM_NO=16_16063_7 | https://hojicha.co/products/hojicha-powder | https://purasana.com/en/hojicha-powder','','Gellatti · GC65 Hojicha Powder closure','2026-09-09'),
('PI-ING-002551','global_rooibos_red_dry_leaf_ground_whole_no_carrier','ROOIBOS · Traditional Red · Dry Leaf / Ground Whole Leaf · No Carrier','Standard','Standard','South Africa','','coffee_tea','herbal_tea_rooibos_dry_leaf','TRUE','TRUE','Estimated / Source-based global reference','SA Rooibos Council identity/process + pure 100% milled Rooibos label + peer-reviewed Rooibos ash study; GC66 explicit mass-balance model','2026-09-09','78','3.83','96.17','1.2','0.79','0','0','5.8','0','16.2','0.6','0','0','0','0','0','0','70.8','0.53','0','2.17','','','96.17','0.6','3.7005','','0.006','0.037004999999999996','0','','','240','','','none_declared','TRUE','TRUE','TRUE','FALSE','ambient_dry','','GLOBAL DEFINED REFERENCE for traditional oxidized red Rooibos. Pure dried Rooibos leaf/stem material or the same whole material after grinding; no sugar, milk, extract carrier or flavour added. Distinct from PI-ING-002489 filtered infusion. If the whole ground material remains in the recipe, count the full retained composition. If Rooibos is steeped and the solids are removed, use the final infusion profile instead. Green unoxidized Rooibos and instant/extracted powders require separate identities. Exact commercial grade, cut and TDS override this reference.','GC66 ENGINE-APPROVED GLOBAL REFERENCE MODEL. A pure milled Rooibos label supplies fat 1.2 g, saturates 0.79 g, protein 5.8 g, fibre 70.8 g, sugars 0.6 g, salt 0.53 g and energy 240 kcal per 100 g. The label''s carbohydrate 87 g is interpreted as total carbohydrate including fibre because using 16.2 g available carbohydrate (87-70.8) reconciles both mass and declared energy; this interpretation is explicit, not a universal label rule. Ash 2.17 g comes from a peer-reviewed Rooibos tea analysis. Water 3.83 g is the residual mass-balance model, not a batch moisture assay. Salt is contained within ash and is not added twice to mass. Sugar species are not declared; POD/PAC treat aggregate sugars as sucrose-equivalent plus the existing salt factor. Polyphenols and other Rooibos solids receive no additional guessed PAC. The nutrition label used is a wild milled grade, so exact cultivated commercial material may differ and always overrides this global prior.','https://sarooibos.co.za/frequently-asked-questions/ | https://nazanitea.com/products/rooibos-gemaalcha | https://doi.org/10.1108/BFJ-07-2019-0568 | https://itematlas.com.au/details_product/organic-rooibos-aspalathus-linearis-tea-cut','','Gellatti · GC66 Dry Rooibos closure','2026-09-09'),
